<p>These terms govern the use of Rendetto. By registering an account you accept them.</p>

<h2>Who provides the service</h2>
<p><%= company.name %>, company number (EIK) <%= company.eik %>, VAT number <%= company.vat %>, ul. Samuil 3, <%= company.postalCode %> Bobov Dol, Kyustendil Province, Bulgaria. Contact: <a href="mailto:<%= contact %>"><%= contact %></a>.</p>

<h2>What Rendetto is</h2>
<p>Rendetto is browser software for designing panel furniture. From one project it calculates a 3D model, a cut list with edge banding, a hardware list, drawings with a drilling map and files for a CNC machine (DXF and G-code). Everything is calculated from the data you enter and from the hardware manufacturers' documentation.</p>

<h2>Account</h2>
<ul>
  <li>An account is personal: do not share it. Create a separate account for each person on your team.</li>
  <li>Use a real email address — confirmations, new passwords and security warnings go there.</li>
  <li>Keep your password safe. You can turn on two-factor protection under “Security” in your account.</li>
  <li>If you suspect someone else has access, change your password and write to us.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Trial</h2>
<p>Every new account gets a <%= trialDays %>-day trial from the moment the email is confirmed, with all features. We do not ask for payment details. There is one trial per person or company: several accounts for more trials are not allowed and may be blocked.</p>

<h2>Plans and prices</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Premium: €25 per month excluding VAT. Paying for 3, 6 or 12 months at once gives a 5%, 10% or 20% discount.</li>
  <li>Lifetime: €750 excluding VAT, one payment — 2.5 times the yearly price without the 12-month discount. It does not expire for as long as we offer Rendetto.</li>
  <li>VAT is charged according to the rules for the buyer's country; in Bulgaria it is 20%.</li>
  <li>We may change prices for future periods. A period already paid for does not change.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Payment and activation</h2>
<p>You request a plan under “Plan” in your account. We send you payment details and an invoice. The plan is activated manually once the payment arrives, and you get an email. If you pay while your trial or paid period is still running, the new months start after it ends.</p>

<h2>When the plan ends</h2>
<p>After the trial or paid period ends, the account stays and its projects can still be opened and downloaded in every format. New projects, saving changes and copying projects need an active plan. You can always delete projects.</p>

<h2>Right of withdrawal</h2>
<p>If you are a consumer, you can withdraw from a paid plan within 14 days of payment without giving a reason, by writing to <a href="mailto:<%= contact %>"><%= contact %></a>. If, at your request, the plan started before that period ended, you owe the part of the price for the time it was active; we refund the rest within 14 days. The right of withdrawal does not apply to purchases by businesses.</p>

<h2>What is not allowed</h2>
<ul>
  <li>getting around the security, the plan limits or the trial;</li>
  <li>automated mass requests and attempts to overload the service;</li>
  <li>attempts to access other people's accounts or data;</li>
  <li>unlawful or offensive content in project names.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Blocking</h2>
<p>If these terms are breached, we may block an account. The reason is shown when you try to sign in. If you think the block is a mistake, write to us — if it is, we restore access.</p>

<h2>Outputs and liability</h2>
<p class="disclaimer">Rendetto calculates from the data you enter. Before production, check the sizes, the construction and the drawings, and run the G-code first in a simulation and as a dry run: the post-processors are generic and do not know your particular machine. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for material, tools or machines damaged by using outputs that were not checked. Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law does not allow to be limited, for example for damage caused intentionally or by gross negligence. If you are a consumer, you also keep your legal rights when the service does not conform to the contract.</p>

<h2>Availability</h2>
<p>We aim to keep Rendetto running without interruption but do not guarantee it: there is occasional maintenance. Keep important projects as downloaded files too.</p>

<h2>Rights in the software and the projects</h2>
<p>The software, its design and the catalogues in it belong to <%= company.name %>. Your projects and their outputs are yours. We store and process projects only to provide the service — details in the <a href="<%= legalPath(locale, 'privacy') %>">privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>For a material change we will write to you at least 30 days before it takes effect. If you do not agree, you can stop using Rendetto and delete your account.</p>

<h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
<p>Bulgarian law applies. Disputes are settled by the competent Bulgarian court. If you are a consumer, you keep the protection of the mandatory rules of the country where you live, and you can turn to the Bulgarian Commission for Consumer Protection and to its general conciliation commissions for out-of-court settlement of the dispute (<a href="https://www.kzp.bg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.kzp.bg</a>).</p>
